 "_doc": "Build analyte_groups from the app's biomarker dedupe table (spec v1.8 10g.1). Data, not rules.\n\nspelling groups: every inventory id of one analyte; a bare name reads them all in one read.\nunit_split groups (legacy id + %/absolute ids): the legacy/bare id expands to all present; a specific id stays specific.\nsampling_split groups (spec v1.8 10g.27): same semantics as unit_split for a sampling condition of one analyte: bare \"glucose\"\nreads every present id of {glucose, fasting_glucose}, \"fasting glucose\" stays fasting_glucose. The app aliases bare glucose to\nfasting_glucose, so these ids are taken out of the spelling groups.",
